     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hello!<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am using the lavaan package in R. In particular, I am trying modelling my data with the Structural Equation Model (SEM) but, since it’s the first time for me with this analysis, I would like to ask feedback about the output of the model. <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am most interested in the regression part of the model:  I have 2 dependent variables (VD1 and VD2) based on ratings (continuous values from (0 to 6), and I have an independent variable (VI1), that is categorical (binomial values, present/absent). <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">My model is:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">Model1 &lt;-‘VD1~VI1<u></u><u></u></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">VD2~VI1’<u></u><u></u></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I then estimate the model with this command: <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">Model1.fit &lt;- sem(Model1, data=dat) <u></u><u></u></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">And extracted the results with this command:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">summary(Model1.fit, standardized = TRUE, rsq = T, fit.measures=TRUE)<u></u><u></u></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I used this command for the plot:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">semPaths(Model1.fit, &quot;par&quot;, edge.label.cex = 0.9, curvePivot = TRUE, layout = &quot;tree&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">The follow is the output of the model:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lavaan (0.5-23.1097) converged normally after  22 iterations<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:medium;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"426\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:-webkit-standard;width:319.85pt;border-collapse:collapse\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">  Number of observations                           794<u></u><u></u></p></td></tr><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"></td></tr><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.000