   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>Your model is saturated (degrees of freedom = 0), which means that it cannot be tested. Model testing requires that you have a surplus of information, and the consistency of that surplus information with the estimated model provides a way of testing model fit. </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/post/How_to_test_saturated_path_models_using_SEM1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.researchgate.net/post/How_to_test_saturated_path_models_using_SEM1&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792425717841000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1_wz982bbPaPukhLrtGIBs\">https://www.researchgate.net/post/How_to_test_saturated_path_models_using_SEM1</a></div><div><br></div><div>Mikko<br><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>On 18 Apr 2018, at 12.17, Giuliana Sorrentino &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">giuliana....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:</div><br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Hello!<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am using the lavaan package in R. In particular, I am trying modelling my data with the Structural Equation Model (SEM) but, since it’s the first time for me with this analysis, I would like to ask feedback about the output of the model. <u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I am most interested in the regression part of the model:  I have 2 dependent variables (VD1 and VD2) based on ratings (continuous values from (0 to 6), and I have an independent variable (VI1), that is categorical (binomial values, present/absent). <u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">My model is:<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">Model1 &lt;-‘VD1~VI1<u></u><u></u></span></b></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">VD2~VI1’<u></u><u></u></span></b></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I then estimate the model with this command: <u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">Model1.fit &lt;- sem(Model1, data=dat) <u></u><u></u></span></b></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">And extracted the results with this command:<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">summary(Model1.fit, standardized = TRUE, rsq = T, fit.measures=TRUE)<u></u><u></u></span></b></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">I used this command for the plot:<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">semPaths(Model1.fit, &quot;par&quot;, edge.label.cex = 0.9, curvePivot = TRUE, layout = &quot;tree&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></b></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">The follow is the output of the model:<u></u><u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">lavaan (0.5-23.1097) converged normally after  22 iterations<u></u><u></u></div><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:inherit;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><u></u> <u></u></span></div><table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" width=\"426\" style=\"font-family:-webkit-standard;width:319.85pt;border-collapse:collapse\"><tbody><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">  Number of observations                           794<u></u><u></u></div></td></tr><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"></td></tr><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">  Estimator                                                        ML<u></u><u></u></div></td></tr><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">  Minimum Function Test Statistic                0.000<u></u><u></u></div></td></tr><tr style=\"height:16pt\"><td width=\"426\" nowrap valign=\"bottom\" style=\"width:319.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt;height:16pt\"><div style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\">  Degrees of freedom                                      0<u></u><u></u></div></td></tr><tr